# Assets embedded with `include_bytes!`/`include_dir!` and base64'd into
# diagram and report output. git rewrites text files to CRLF on a Windows
# checkout, which changes the bytes, which changes the base64, which fails the
# golden files on Windows and only on Windows. Keep them byte-for-byte.
#
# The emitters normalise line endings anyway (`src/mark.rs`), because this only
# governs checkout — but there is no reason for the bytes to differ at all.
*.svg -text
*.png -text
*.ttf -text
*.otf -text

# Golden files are compared byte-for-byte across Linux, macOS and Windows.
*.snap -text

# Bundled KQL is embedded and hashed as executed query provenance. Windows
# checkout conversion must not change those bytes or the report golden hashes.
queries/**/*.toml text eol=lf
